  "strategy": "Approach and rationale:\nWe'll implement a Progressive Boosted Optimization algorithm that focuses on improving a base solution through iterative refinements. \nThe approach combines three key elements:\n1. Starting with a strong base solution (periodic cosine initialization)\n2. Using Frank-Wolfe iterations with adaptive thresholding to enhance it locally\n3. Gradually expanding the sequence length as an explicit secondary objective\n\nOur rationale is:\n- The periodic cosine base solution provides a good starting point\n- Frank-Wolfe with adaptive thresholds avoids getting stuck in local minima found by standard LP projections\n- Gradually lengthening the sequence allows us to incorporate more structure while maintaining non-negativity\n\nWe believe this approach will find better solutions because:\n- The base solution captures important periodic structures\n- The Frank-Wolfe refinement continues until local stability is reached\n- The length expansion moves us to denser, more complex sequences - essentially transitioning through discrete resolutions\n\nMathematical specification:\nWe consider sequences of the form x = [x\u2080, ..., x_{n-1}], x\u1d62 \u2265 0.\nThe objective J(x) = (2*n*max(convolve(x,x,mode='full'))) / (sum(x))\u00b2\n\nOur algorithm consists of:\n1. Base initialization with cosine\n2. Frank-Wolfe optimization with inexact solver and adaptive active set\n3. Secondary objective: incremental sequence lengthening\n\nImplementation procedure:\n1. Validate input and initialize n=8192 (maximum considered length)\n\nThe evaluation function will be bound by:\n- Time budget management throughout iterations\n- Non-periodic (linear) convolution with full mode\n- Cosine initialization as a strong starting candidate\n\nLet's define the algorithm with careful steps:\n\ndef propose_candidate():\n    # Implementation details\n    import numpy as np\n    import time\n    \n    # Check parent sequence if available\n    parent_sequence = get_parent_sequence()\n    \n    # Base configuration\n    base_sequence_length = 8192\n    best_solution = prepare_cosine_init(base_sequence_length)\n    best_score = evaluate_sequence(best_solution)\n    best_time = time.time()\n    \n    # Adam/K-Fac optimizer configuration\n    num_epochs = 10\n    batch_size = 512\n    decay_rate = 0.9\n    learning_rate = 0.05\n    stopping_threshold = 0.001\n    \n    for epoch in range(num_epochs):\n        # Dynamic time budget allocation based on remaining time\n        current_time = time.time()\n        remaining_time = budget_s - current_time\n        \n        # Calculate step time budget as gamma*remaining_time\n        step_budget = remaining_time * 0.8 - shift_time_penalty(5)\n        \n        if step_budget <= 0:\n            break\n            \n        # Perform gradient-based refinement\n        refine_output = frank_wolfe_refine(best_solution, best_score, step_budget)\n        new_best = refine_output[0]\n        new_score = refine_output[1]\n        \n        if new_score < best_score:\n            best_score = new_score\n            best_solution = new_solution.copy()\n            best_time = time.time()\n            print(f\"Epoch {epoch}: Improved solution with score {best_score}\")\n        else:\n            print(f\"Epoch {epoch}: No improvement, abandoning refinement\")\n            \n        # Conditional lengthening step if time permits and we're below 4K\n        if time.time() - best_time < stopping_threshold and len(best_solution) < 8192:\n            if remaining_time > step_budget + 2.0:\n                lengthen_sequence(best_solution, remaining_time)\n    \n    # Fallback strategy\n    if np.isnan(best_score) or best_score > 7.0:\n        # Revert to period doubling with multiple restarts\n        restart_count = 3\n        for i in range(restart_count):\n            if i % 2 == 0:\n                new_init = cosine_init(8192 * (9/16))\n            else:\n                new_init = sine_init(8192 * (7/8))\n            new_seq = np.asarray(new_init)\n            score = evaluate_sequence(new_seq)\n            if score < best_score:\n                best_solution = new_seq.copy()\n                best_score = score\n                best_time = time.time()\n            else:\n                fuzzy_restart(best_solution)\n                \n    elif no_finite_solution_found(best_score):\n        # Structure-based perturbation\n        perturb_amplitude = 0.07 * (1 + i)\n        new_solution = structure_perturb(best_solution, perturb_amplitude)\n        best_score = evaluate_sequence(new_solution)\n        best_solution = new_solution.copy()\n    \n    # Return best solution\n    process_final_output(best_solution, best_score)\n    return best_solution.tolist()",
